    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456-a1">

                <pb facs="0551" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg463"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I have received the note, dated
                    yesterday, in which your excellency was pleased to inform me that, according to
                    a telegram from the consul of the United States at Matamoros, Messrs. H. C.
                    Harding and H. E. Dugat, accused in the said city of infraction of the fiscal
                    laws, are still in prison.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to say to your excellency that I have sent a copy of
                    the said note to the department of the treasury repeating the request which I
                    had made before and of which I informed the embassy in my note of the 14th
                    instant.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
